class.description:
A dialogue line node holds one line of a dialogue: the [member speaker], the [member text] and optionally a [member voice] recording and a [member subtitle]. It has the flow input [code]in[/code] and the flow output [code]out[/code].
At runtime the node waits ([constant FlowGraphPlayback.ENTER_RESULT_WAIT]). The game's dialogue UI shows the line when [signal FlowGraphPlayback.node_waiting] reports it and calls [method FlowGraphPlayback.advance] when the player continues. The engine has no dialogue UI node; the game builds its own. Because the waiting state lives in the playback, [method FlowGraphPlayback.set_state] shows the same line again after loading a savegame.
[b]Translation.[/b] [member text] is either the sentence itself or a translation key such as [code]SHOP_HELLO[/code] for a CSV translation. [method get_translated_text] translates it with [method Object.tr] and [member translation_context]. The texts of a graph saved as [code].tres[/code], [code].res[/code] or [code].mmd[/code] are collected by the POT generation of the project settings (Localization > POT Generation). Text with variables is formatted by the UI, for example with [method String.format] and the blackboard variables.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _on_node_waiting(node_id: int, node: FlowNode) -> void:
	if node is DialogueLineNode:
		name_label.text = node.get_translated_speaker_name()
		text_label.text = node.get_translated_text().format(playback.get_blackboard().variables)
		if node.voice:
			voice_player.stream = node.voice
			voice_player.play()

func _on_continue_pressed() -> void:
	playback.advance()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private void OnNodeWaiting(long nodeId, FlowNode node)
{
	if (node is DialogueLineNode line)
	{
		_nameLabel.Text = line.GetTranslatedSpeakerName();
		_textLabel.Text = line.GetTranslatedText();
	}
}

private void OnContinuePressed()
{
	_playback.Advance();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
